BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"UC Davis Library": "https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/maptimedavis-map-design-cartography"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:maptimeDavis: Map Design & Cartography
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260515T120000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52497887387598
DESCRIPTION:Description: Making a map that communicates well is difficult.
  You likely spent a significant amount of time and energy planning and imp
 lementing your analysis and you want the resulting map to reflect that. In
  this workshop\, we'll learn some guidelines for map visualilzations that 
 communicate your intended message quickly and accurately. We'll work in QG
 IS\, but the concepts you learn in this workshop will apply to any map-mak
 ing software and even to non-map figures like graphs.\n\n \n\nConcepts Cov
 ered: Cartography\, Figure Design\, Visual Hierarchy\n\n \n\nSpeaker: Mich
 ele Tobias\n\n \n\nMichele Tobias is a geospatial data scientist with a ba
 ckground in geospatial methods for ecology. Michele earned her PhD from UC
  Davis in Geography where she studied California’s sandy beach ecosystem
  with traditional phytosociological methods and innovative remote sensing 
 tools and was a postdoc at the UC Davis Information Center for the Environ
 ment. In her current position as a geospatial data scientist at UC Davis D
 ataLab\, she applies geospatial tools to new avenues of research across di
 sciplines.\n \n\nPrerequisites: No prior experience is required\, but fami
 liarity with spatial data formats (raster and vector) is recommended.\n\n 
 \n\nSoftware Required: QGIS: available for all major computer operating sy
 stems at qgis.org\n\n \n\nPlease RSVP.
LOCATION:DataLab\, 360 Shields Library
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/maptimedavis-map-design-carto
 graphy
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
