DESCRIPTION:Do you have questions about the election? Where do the governo
 r candidates stand on the issues? What does the insurance commissioner do?
 \n\nPlease join us on May 22 as we welcome the nonprofit statewide publica
 tion CalMatters as they breakdown\, analyze and answer your burning ques
 tions about this year’s primary election\, in a conversation centered ar
 ound the latest edition of their Voter Guide.\n\nFeatured guests include A
 bridged by PBS KVIE’s Yolo County reporter Daniel Hennessy and Executive
  Director of Davis Media Access Autumn Labbe-Renault.\n\nThe local iterati
 on of this event is sponsored by the Yolo County Library.\n\n\n	Doors open
  at 5:30PM\n	Introduction\, trivia\, local partners speak\, main portion t
 o discuss issues\, closing\n	Tickets are free\, but seating is limited\n	T
 he event will be held from 6 p.m. to 7:30 p.m. on Friday\, May 22\, inside
  the Blanchard Room at the Mary L. Stephens-Davis Branch Library.\n	Food w
 ill be provided by CalMatters\n\n\nBy reserving a ticket\, you agree to re
 ceive occasional marketing updates from Abridged by PBS KVIE.\n\nReserve y
 our ticket here: Eventbrite
LOCATION:Blanchard Room\, Small Conference Room\, Mary L Stephens Davis Br
 anch Library
URL:https://events.yolocountylibrary.org/event/16878552
X-SOURCE:Yolo Library
END:VEVENT
