X-SOURCE-ID:ucdavis_library
SUMMARY:maptimeDavis: Spatial SQL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T120000
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52497914121538
DESCRIPTION:Description: This workshop is intended to give participants an
  introduction to working with spatial data using SQL -- a database queryin
 g language. We will work with a graphical user interface (GUI) and explore
  some examples of common analysis processes as well as present participant
 s with resources for continued learning. This workshop will give participa
 nts a solid foundation on which to build further learning. By the end of t
 his workshop\, participants will be able to import data into a spatialite 
 database\, write queries to answer questions about spatial data\, understa
 nd the difference between attribute queries and geometry queries\, view sp
 atial tables and views in QGIS\, and use terminology related to spatial da
 tabases to facilitate future learning.\n\n \n\nConcepts Covered: Databases
 \, SQL\, Spatial Analysis\, Data Management\n\n \n\nSpeakers: Alex Mandel\
 , Michele Tobias\, Naomi Kalman\, Holden Tal\n\n \n\nThis workshop will be
  taught by a team of instructors who use spatial SQL in their work and res
 earch.\n\n \n\nPrerequisites: No prior experience is required\, but famili
 arity with spatial data formats (raster and vector) is recommended.\n\n \n
 \nSoftware Required: QGIS: available for all major computer operating syst
 ems at qgis.org\n\n \n\nPlease RSVP.
LOCATION:DataLab\, 360 Shields Library
URL:https://events.library.ucdavis.edu/event/maptimedavis-spatial-sql
X-SOURCE:UC Davis Library
END:VEVENT
